dispose patients to this complication</article-title><source>Psychosomatics</source><year>1987</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>93</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3432529</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Riley</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></name><name><surname>Pleet</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Stewart</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Multiple entrapment neuropathies in depression</article-title><source>Journal of Clinical Psychiatry</source><year>1980</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>214</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7380821</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>American Psychiatric Association</collab></person-group><source>diagnostic and statistical manual of mental disorders, (DSM-IV)</source><year>1994</year><edition>fourth</edition><publisher-name>Washington DC, American Psychiatric Association</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dyck</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Detection, characterization, and staging of polyneuropathy: Assessed in diabetics</article-title><source>Muscle &#x00026; Nerve</source><year>1988</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>21</fpage><lpage>32</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3277049</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/mus.880110106</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>American Association of Electrodiagnostic Medicine</collab></person-group><article-title>Consensus criteria for the diagnosis of partial conduction block</article-title><source>Muscle Nerve Suppl</source><year>1999</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>S225</fpage><